WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.040
Finally, someplace that has that
"home of a serial killer" atmosphere.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.750
His victims included a pro
wrestler and a martial artist.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.620
It makes you wonder whether he
really defeated them one-on-one.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.620
This "Challenger"... Katsuyama Denshin.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.500
If the fights had been normal matches, sure.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:35.080
But fairly few can react right away when
they realize someone's trying to kill them.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.580
Besides...

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.290
The Challenger didn't exactly prize fair fights.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.750
Narihisago's daughter.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.870
It was one-sided and barbaric.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.830
Not only had he brutally lost his only daughter,

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.120
his wife had also committed suicide.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.000
That bastard Narihisago.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.120
He really did unload the moment he walked in.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:30.580
This is Matsuoka. Cognition
particles gleaned from the scene.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.080
They're Narihisago's.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.950
Confirmed.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.000
I know the building was locked down,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.910
but even three years later
the readings are massive.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.370
That's one hell of a drive to kill.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.830
There's a stairway hidden behind the curtain.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.950
Take it to the underground level.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.750
The hidden mics and cameras from Fukuda's home.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.290
Any progress?

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.410
They're checking the access logs.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.000
It involves multiple foreign servers,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.120
so progress seems stalled.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.830
Turning the power on.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.830
So this is the Challenger's arena.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.080
Sorry. It was an accident.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.160
Got the Challenger's particles, too.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.410
Confirmed.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.080
Is Narihisago doing these?

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.580
No, I'll have Hondomachi do it.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.580
Her?

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.830
So soon?

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:48.790
Yes. With the precedent Fukuda set,
we need to see whether she can perform.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.870
Well, true.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.500
I guarantee she's capable.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.120
She's not simply an excellent investigator.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.540
She's something else.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.870
Momoki.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.370
About Hondomachi.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.870
Take care of her.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.200
Of course.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.540
Bye.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.500
That's the situation, Hondomachi.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.700
Do your stuff.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.950
I'll do my best.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.540
As predicted, the figure of John Walker
appeared within the Challenger's well.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:55.500
By all appearances, John Walker set his sights
on Kazuta Haruka and Fukuda Tamotsu

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.040
while he was surveilling Inami Nahoshi.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.290
Likewise, he may have been
searching for his next serial killer

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:05.950
while he was surveilling the Challenger, Denshin Katsuyama.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:13.100
Furthermore, the only people who entered
Katsuyama's house were Katsuyama's victims

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.290
and the man who shot him,
then officer Narihisago Akihito.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.000
But Narihisago shot the Challenger
immediately at the door, right?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.410
Doesn't that rule out John Walker
influencing Narihisago's crime?

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.830
There's a chance John Walker had already
set his sights on Narihisago Akihito

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:35.200
when Narihisago Muku
fell victim to the Challenger.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.790
I see.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:42.450
Still, that would mean that John Walker
not only turned Narihisago into a serial killer,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:47.200
but also created the serial killer
that murdered his daughter.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.750
We don't know for sure.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:53.000
We'll have to take a look at Narihisago's id well.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.040
Let's see this through.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.870
So many...

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.330
I have to get out of here, too!

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:01.370
I know this dead girl's name.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.660
This is Kaeru.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:07.080
And so I remember who I am.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.620
My name is Hijiriido Miyo...

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.160
...the brilliant detective.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.330
Why is she the only one with a full name?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.450
All right. Proceed as normal.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.830
Togo, take general analysis. Kokufu, assist Togo.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.950
Shiratake, ascertain periods and locations.
Habutae, analyze the people.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.700
Wakashika...

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:32.660
...you're on mystery duty
with the brilliant detective.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.910
Director?

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:35.200
Sorry.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.620
I just...

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.410
It's Narihisago's wife and daughter, isn't it?

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:42.750
Yeah.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:55.370
Seriously? Men and women in the same cell block?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:58.620
I recommend you file a grievance, young lady.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.250
This was at my request.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:09.290
How did you get that hole?

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.080
How do you think?

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.620
Someone did that to you?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.080
I did it myself.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.700
Yourself?

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.500
It's possible to do that without dying?

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.370
Most people do die.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.410
I just got lucky.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:31.620
Well, there are two others who survived,
so maybe I'm not especially lucky.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.080
You did that to others, too?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.370
Have you met someone else with a hole?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.160
Two, as a matter of fact.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.870
One was someone important to me.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:49.250
And? Because of the hole, things didn't work out?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.410
Thanks to the hole, we might have
managed to connect in the end.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.500
Holes bring liberation, you see.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.040
But...

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.290
...the second one killed him.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.750
Is that what happened?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:12.080
The little lady's really working overtime, isn't she?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.750
With the Mizuhanome, suicide counts as killing.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.540
That means in the past month,

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:28.870
she's been involved in at least two
killings and arrested a serial killer.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.330
Assuming she was chosen as a new detective

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:35.410
because she has the aptitude
and can enter the Mizuhanome...

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.370
If she's diving this very moment...

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.040
That would mean it's my well?!

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.830
Not just that.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.580
Is there a chance <i>he </i>will appear in my well?!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.080
What is he doing?

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:56.870
I don't know exactly, but I think he needs to rethink all that thinking he does.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:02.040
John Walker!

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.790
The number of people in view at present is 358.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.450
The number of casualties is 175.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:17.660
They're all Narihisago's family,
relatives, former classmates, or the like.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:21.660
There have been seven thunderbolts
so far since Hijiriido arrived,

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:27.660
but we could only see which numbers were
hit for the first, third, and seventh strikes.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:32.500
Those were 5, 3, and 8. As of yet this sequence of numbers means nothing.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.290
What about John Walker?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.040
Nothing so far.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:43.250
Does this sequence represent
the randomness of lightning?

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.290
Where's the key?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.950
Come on! Why?!

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.160
Are you taking me down with you?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:00.540
I'm not here to die.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.660
But neither am I here to survive.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:07.160
Escaping the lightning isn't my task.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.330
I'm here to solve the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.790
The mystery...

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.450
In concrete terms...

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:18.750
"Why is Kaeru handcuffed dead to my arm?"

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.290
Yes.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.580
Did Kaeru put the cuffs on me?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.080
No. That can't be.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.950
If she had put the cuffs on me,

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:31.910
I too would have died when she was struck.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:34.660
Some other person put them on me.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.330
For what purpose?

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.120
I got it.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:57.790
It was him.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.870
Aki!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.950
Dad! Where are you?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.870
What good will that do?

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:19.790
That's not going to make
that machine respond at all.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:22.700
Even if I die, my id well won't disappear.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.290
And I can't stop the Mizuhanome either.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.790
For now just calm down, Brother.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.660
Shut your trap!

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:32.700
What's going on with these people?

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:40.120
These handcuffs were put on after Kaeru died.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:43.870
To make it so I wouldn't move from this spot.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:50.620
Most likely this man believed lightning
doesn't strike the same place twice.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.830
But that's just a perception he had.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:57.120
In actuality, the probability of
lighting striking a particular spot

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:00.120
shouldn't change much.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:06.200
It's perfectly possible for real lightning to strike the same place twice.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.620
For real lightning.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.080
But this is different.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.370
It's incredibly close to real lightning, but it's not.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.790
It's fake.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.750
One,

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:19.830
two,

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:20.910
three,

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.040
four,

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:22.950
five,

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:23.910
six,

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:24.830
seven,

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:25.750
eight,

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:27.040
nine.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.080
One,

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.120
two,

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.160
three,

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.290
four,

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.290
five,

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.250
six,

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.200
seven,

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.200
eight,

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.120
nine.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.370
I knew it!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:41.080
It only feels random thanks to the variation in distance

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.370
changing the intervals between thunderclaps.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:47.200
But really the timing of the strikes is constant.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.410
It's about nine seconds between flashes.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.450
In short, this isn't natural lightning.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.500
It's artificial.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.870
It's plenty possible it wouldn't strike twice.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:02.700
That is precisely why I am being kept here.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:07.000
Further, no one else has realized the truth.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.870
Why didn't he tell the others?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.830
I don't know.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:19.450
Whatever the case may be, he saved
me first and was then struck himself.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.160
But, there's something I can do.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.910
Everyone listen!

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.370
Listen to me!

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.330
Pass this on!

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:45.540
You're safe!

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:49.370
This lighting won't strike the same place twice!

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.200
One,

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.160
two,

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:08.200
three,

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.200
four,

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.200
five,

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.200
six,

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.160
seven,

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.290
eight,

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.370
nine.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:23.040
During each nine seconds,
I can move between the panels!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.700
Don't worry.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:32.750
As long as you stick to places the
lightning has already struck, it'll be fine.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.160
"Fine"?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.000
How long is this going to continue?

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.830
I can't say.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:44.540
But as long as it continues, the
safe territory will gradually expand.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.620
But look!

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.540
People are dying over there, too!

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:51.870
How are we going to help them?

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:55.700
Well, this isn't exactly a nice way of putting it,

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:57.950
but I'm a brilliant detective.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:02.830
I'm here to solve mysteries,
not to save people, you see.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.790
I've already informed you
how the lightning works,

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.370
so if you're concerned about those people,

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.200
I believe <i>you </i>could go to them.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:15.540
After all, I expect we have roughly the same amount of stamina.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:22.500
I suppose Hijiriido is right,
but she's kinda cold, isn't she?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:26.540
Even brilliant detectives have their quirks.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.000
Mom.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.120
This lady is exactly right.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:32.250
We have to try, too.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.620
She told us how to escape the lightning.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:37.870
Now it's up to <i>us</i> to make
this world a better place!

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.330
Muku.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.000
I swear.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.540
She's just like the real Muku.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.250
Yep. You're right. We all
have to do our parts, right?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.750
Well, I need to move.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.250
Goodbye.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:59.200
Thanks, Ms. Detective!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.500
Ms. um...

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.500
Hijiriido Miyo.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.830
That's...

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:16.950
A cockpit!

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:17.910
How?!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.750
The Kura launched one year ago!

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.160
This well is from three years ago!

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.410
A cockpit is in operation...

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.160
Is this id well linked via the Mizuhanome

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:30.290
to Narihisago's unconscious in the present?

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:31.660
It appears so.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:35.000
The update's in progress, present progressive...

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.540
Now then. What's next?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.120
What is... this?

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.830
Asukai Kiki!

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.660
Habutae, who is that?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.250
The Challenger's last victim.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:06.000
After Narihisago murdered
the Challenger... I rescued her.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.160
Director?

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.450
I've looked for her since...

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.200
I never imagined I'd see her name here.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.660
This is bad.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.500
Togo, prepare to extract.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.580
Don't move! Stay where you are!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.750
What?

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.000
We're mid-investigation! Get out!

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:35.250
Please obey these investigators' instructions.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.540
Chief.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:40.620
Momoki Funetaro, you are
suspected of inducing murder.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.120
Inducement? Just who did I induce?

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:48.290
At least six serial killers. That's who.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.500
Mr. Momoki.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.330
<i>You're </i>John Walker.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:56.450
We analyzed the data from the mics and cameras from Fukuda's house.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:19:00.450
We confirmed several instances
of access from your computer.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.580
That can't be!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.950
It must be a mistake!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.080
No, this is a complete setup!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.870
A body was just discovered at this man's house.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:13.450
We also need to question him
as a material witness for that.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.330
Look.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:18.370
This is Momoki's yard.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.950
The DNA results came back.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.830
It's Shirakoma Nishio.

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:28.620
As you all know, he's the
inventor of the Mizuhanome.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:32.200
Momoki, you need to explain this.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:34.450
So he was killed?

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.200
What is she doing?!

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.330
Extract!

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.330
I can't!

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:43.830
The apparatus isn't working!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.000
So she's in a well within the well.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.830
Director!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.950
Don't touch anything else. This is an arrest!

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:55.790
I'm relieving Momoki of duty.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:59.500
For the new director, I appoint you, Ms. Togo.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:00.620
But wait!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.200
This is an emergency.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:06.950
For right now, try to save your brilliant detective.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:12.830
Everyone return to your stations!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.500
Hey! Get Forensics here!

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.910
We've found something unbelievable!

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.200
Dammit.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.750
I don't know what's going on anywhere!

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.200
Was John Walker in my id well?

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.620
How did you know we--

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.790
Well?

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:33.790
A brilliant detective even outside the well.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.000
I'll share our conclusions.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.700
John Walker was not found in your id well.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.950
I see.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:46.000
Either way, I just have to keep
taking responsibility for what I did.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:50.080
There's one other thing of
which I must inform you today.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:53.120
It's about Momoki's absence, right?

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.500
No matter what was found in my well,

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:59.790
Momoki would never send
someone else to tell me about it.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:02.580
What happened to Momoki?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.330
The director...

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.620
Momoki was arrested.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.040
On what charges?

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.160
Creating numerous serial killers as John Walker,

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:18.250
and causing at least 44 murders.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:22.540
As well as involvement in the
murder of the Mizuhanome's inventor.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.290
How could...

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:26.500
What's the evidence?

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.080
They have it, right?

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:38.000
A body was discovered buried at his residence.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.330
Hold it!

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:45.950
What is it?

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:53.410
Who knows if I'm too late or just in
time, but I figured out the sequence.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.870
Take a look.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.160
It's a monitor recording.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:00.000
5, 3, 8, 6, 7, 1, 4.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.250
This is only what was within Hijiriido's
field of vision, so I tried something.

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:06.870
Bingo.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.120
It's pi.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.620
Pi, huh?

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:10.910
Yes.

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:15.750
They say every sequence of numbers
appears in pi's endless sequence.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:19.950
Even though they seem random,
the numbers in pi adhere to an order.

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:27.250
And this sequence, 5, 3, 8, 6, 7, 1, 4...

00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:32.750
It first appears at the
10,375,576th digit of pi.

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:36.250
The lightning struck every 9.03 seconds,

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:42.330
so the first lightning strike was
93,691,442.25 seconds prior.

00:22:42.330 --> 00:22:45.870
In other words, 1,084 days ago.

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:46.910
That was...

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:50.620
The day Narihisago's daughter was murdered, right?

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:52.450
You remember the day?

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:54.250
I just guessed.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:56.950
It's not a difficult quiz.

00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.910
I guess not.

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:03.040
Once you have Momoki's well,

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:04.580
I <i>need </i>you...

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:08.040
...to let me dive into it.
